# The system files a release may place, one rule per line: FOLDER KIND NAME.
#
#   exact   the file is named exactly NAME
#   ending  any plain name that ends in NAME and is longer than it
#
# A committed copy of slipway-core's ALLOWED_SYSTEM_FILES (crates/updater/updater-core/src/release/system.rs), in the same
# order. release.py reads it for pack and verify, so `system/` holding a path no rule here names fails the pack, and
# release/check-system-list.sh compares it with slipway's source (the workflow runs that). slipway's privileged helper
# is installed by hand and is not replaced by a release, so a file added here also needs a new helper on every
# computer: change this list only together with slipway, never alone. The four turnstile rules are slipway's
# input-service change (its FINDINGS 25, commit c36aaa0): until the pinned slipway has them, `check-system-list.sh`
# fails against that pin, so this file and the pin move in the same step. /usr/lib/bardo/key-remap/key-remap.toml is the
# desktop's vendor defaults for the keyboard daemon (slipway's 18th rule); /etc/keycap stays the administrator's and
# no release places a file there. bardo-mouse-gestures.service is the touchpad daemon's system unit (owner decision 2026-10-17: a system
# service like keycap), and the two /usr/lib/systemd/user rules are how a user unit named by a row of
# dist/desktop-callers.toml, and the portal frontend's drop-in, reach the computer as plain root-owned files (a link into
# /opt/bardo/current reads as writable to the unit manager's judge, so such a unit never proves `Full`; release/build.sh
# `plain_units`). All three need a new slipway helper on every computer, and slipway's list changes with them, in this order.
/etc/pam.d                 exact   sill
/etc/udev/rules.d          exact   60-bardo-shell-ddc.rules
/etc/modules-load.d        exact   bardo-shell-ddc.conf
/usr/lib/systemd/system    exact   bardo-key-remap.service
/etc/udev/rules.d          exact   70-bardo-key-remap.rules
/etc/polkit-1/rules.d      exact   bardo-key-remap.polkit.rules
/etc/modules-load.d        exact   keycap.conf
/usr/lib/keycap            exact   keycap.toml
/usr/lib/systemd/system    exact   bardo-input-broker.socket
/usr/lib/systemd/system    exact   bardo-input-broker.service
/etc/udev/rules.d          exact   72-bardo-input-broker.rules
/etc/modules-load.d        exact   turnstile.conf
/etc/udev/rules.d          exact   70-bardo-mouse-gestures.rules
/etc/modprobe.d            exact   99-bardo-mouse-gestures.conf
/usr/lib/systemd/system    exact   bardo-mouse-gestures.service
/usr/lib/systemd/user      ending  .service
/usr/lib/systemd/user/xdg-desktop-portal.service.d exact 10-bardo.conf
/etc/porter                exact   callers.toml
/etc/porter                exact   inferd-callers.toml
/etc/bardo                 ending  -callers.toml
/etc/xdg/bardo             ending  .toml
